VulkanMod-shaded

An unofficial modified build of VulkanMod Reforged, itself an unofficial
modified fork of VulkanMod:
https://github.com/xCollateral/VulkanMod
https://github.com/TrulyRin/VulkanMod-Reforged

Original authors: xCollateral and the VulkanMod contributors.
VulkanMod Reforged maintainer and contributed modifications: Rindw (TrulyRin).

VulkanMod Reforged was modified on 2026-06-19 for NeoForge compatibility and
release metadata. Further renderer, compatibility, and publication changes
were made through 2026-10-22.

VulkanMod-shaded is a further modified version, changed from 2026-10-17 to
2026-10-25 by mockmock69401. This branch ports those changes to VulkanMod
Reforged's Minecraft 1.21.1 (NeoForge) code, on 2026-10-25. The changes
were written with an AI coding assistant (Anthropic's Claude, through
Claude Code) under mockmock69401's direction and testing. They:

- merge the vulkanfix compatibility add-on (package dev.vulkanfix, mixin
  config vulkanfix.mixins.json) and patch the vertex normal packing and the
  shader converter (net.vulkanmod.vulkan.shader.parser) directly; the
  converter also gains geometry stages, interface blocks and uniforms
  declared in imported files, and the pipeline a geometry stage;
- add post-processing (package net.vulkanmod.visuals and
  assets/vulkanmod/visuals), written from requirement documents and
  published graphics literature, with no code from any shader pack;
- add Distant Horizons LOD rendering through the Distant Horizons render API,
  and for Distant Horizons 3.3.1 to 3.3.4 by taking over its internal render
  definition (package net.vulkanmod.visuals.dh, mixins in
  net.vulkanmod.mixin.visuals.legacydh); the LOD terrain shaders in
  assets/vulkanmod/visuals/shaders/dh are translated from Distant Horizons
  (LGPL-3.0, Copyright (C) 2020 James Seibel);
- add frame generation: a built-in camera-reprojection generator ("Optical
  Flow", package net.vulkanmod.visuals.framegen) and AMD FSR 3.1 frame
  generation through AMD's FidelityFX SDK v1.1.4 (package
  net.vulkanmod.visuals.fsr), whose prebuilt signed library is included
  unmodified under its MIT licence;
- add renderer performance and stability fixes found while testing large
  modpacks.

